      "body": "## Overview\n\n`vllm bench mm-processor --dataset-name hf`, the HuggingFace example in `docs/benchmarking/cli.md`, crashes with `AttributeError`. This one-line fix closes the same kind of gap as #56300, which fixed random-mm sampling.\n\n## Claims\n\n`bench mm-processor` runs on HF datasets. `bench throughput` and `bench serve` behave as before.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\nvllm bench mm-processor --model Qwen/Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct --dataset-name hf \\\n  --dataset-path lmarena-ai/VisionArena-Chat --hf-split train --num-prompts 5 --seed 0 \\\n  --load-format dummy --enforce-eager --disable-tqdm --output-json out.json\n\npytest tests/benchmarks/test_throughput_cli.py -k hf_dataset_with_mm_processor\n```\n\n```text\n# before\nAttributeError: 'Namespace' object has no attribute 'hf_name'    # both commands\n\n# after\nbench: exit 0, completed 5, failed 0, 5 encoder calls\npytest: 1 passed\n```\n\nThe bench ran on an L4 with real VisionArena data and dummy weights, on a pinned wheel with the same bug and the same one-line change. The new test uses the real `VisionArenaDataset` with only the HF download stubbed, and checks for text and image chat prompts.\n\n## Details\n\n`get_samples` reads `args.hf_name` for every HF dataset. `bench mm-processor` has no `--hf-name` flag, and `_to_serve_args` backfills its other missing flags but not this one. With `None`, datasets fall back to `--dataset-path`.\n\n`bench mm-processor` still accepts only its listed dataset paths, so local copies stay unsupported. I found no open PR or issue for this.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
